### Demo 3 — one API, three databases
@host = http://localhost:5000

### health — one entry per named data source, each with its own status and timing
GET {{host}}/health

### on-premises SQL Server
GET {{host}}/api/policies?$first=3

### Azure SQL
GET {{host}}/api/claims

### SQL database in Microsoft Fabric
GET {{host}}/api/sales-fact?$filter=period eq '2026-02'
GET {{host}}/api/sales-by-region?$orderby=written_premium desc

### one OpenAPI document covering all three
GET {{host}}/api/openapi

### GraphQL: two sources in one round trip — but two separate queries,
### because DAB does not join across data sources.
POST {{host}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { policies(first: 3) { items { policy_number product } } salesFacts(first: 3) { items { period region written_premium } } }"
}
